q{<strong>Never answer "fine".</strong> Two sentences, one specific detail, one joke at your own expense. That is the entire weekend recap craft.},
q{<strong>Get one back.</strong> If you asked the room, you answer too — the ritual dies when leaders skip their turn.},
q{<strong>The second question is the friendship.</strong> "Does he negotiate the rent?" turned Priya\'s story into a conversation. Always go one question deeper.},
q{<strong>Jokes convert invitations.</strong> "Second dumpling economics" joined a running group in one sentence. Name their joke back to them.},
q{<strong>Bank it for Monday.</strong> Weekend details are next Monday\'s questions: "did the nephew go bankrupt again?" Continuity is what makes people feel known.},
],
practice => [
{ t => 'Your two-sentence story', p => 'Write this Monday\'s recap: two sentences, one specific detail, one self-deprecating spin. No "fine", no weather.', a => q{The detail test: could someone ask a follow-up question about it? "Went hiking" fails; "got lost hiking and asked a shepherd for directions" invites three. Specific details are conversation doors.} },
