grammar => [
['X is green; Y is amber — band grammar', q{<em>"Football is green band; Marco\'s marriage is amber."</em> — the <strong>[topic] is [band]</strong> frame labels conversations in real time. It also teaches the crucial nuance: <strong>the topic is not the unit — the depth is.</strong> Football stays green; whose marriage bends around football is amber. Label depths, not subjects.}, q{"Football is green band; Marco\'s marriage is amber."——<strong>[话题] is [波段]</strong>句式实时标记对话。它还教了关键细微处：<strong>单位不是话题而是深度。</strong>足球始终绿区；谁的婚姻围绕足球弯曲就是黄区。标记深度，不是主题。}],
['Imperative lore from locals', q{<em>"Match the depth of the person who opened the topic."</em>, <em>"Exit gracefully — refills are always available."</em> — veterans transmit office wisdom as imperatives. Collect them verbatim: <strong>imperatives are how unwritten rules travel</strong>, and repeating one back ("that is going in my notes verbatim") honours the teacher and files the rule.}, q{"Match the depth of the person who opened the topic."、"Exit gracefully — refills are always available."——老手以祈使句传授办公室智慧。逐字收集：<strong>祈使句是潜规则的传播形式</strong>，复述回去（"这句要原文记下"）既致敬了老师又归档了规则。}],
],
tips => [
