['Elena (Tech Lead)', q{<strong>The rotation seat — I am stealing that.</strong> One more craft question: <em>how do you open a table of twelve?</em>}, q{<strong>"注意力轮换位"——我要偷学了。</strong>再问一个手艺问题：<em>12 人的桌怎么开场？</em>}],
['You (New Joiner)', q{<strong>One shared question to the whole table, then dyads take over:</strong> "Everyone — one work-free thing you are looking forward to this month, fifteen seconds each." <em>It gives the quiet people a script and the talkers a container.</em> <strong>After round one, conversation self-organises.</strong>}, q{<strong>先给全桌一个共同问题，然后两两对话接管：</strong>"各位——说一件本月期待的、和工作无关的事，每人 15 秒。"<em>它给安静的人一个脚本，给能说的人一个容器。</em><strong>一轮之后，对话会自我组织。</strong>}],
['Priya (Delivery)', q{<strong>Approved, booked, and I am stealing the fifteen-seconds format for the next offsite.</strong> <em>You realise hosting is just standup craft with food?</em>}, q{<strong>批准、订好，而且下次外出活动我要偷走"每人 15 秒"格式。</strong><em>你意识到主办就是加了食物的站会手艺了吗？</em>}],
