{ t => 'Write your two moves', p => 'Draft (a) your one-drink join for tonight, and (b) your decline for next Friday — real hobby, real hook, zero apology.', a => q{Test the decline against Elena\'s grammar: reason in present continuous, hook as imperative on the team, no "sorry" anywhere. "Sorry I will miss it" buys nothing and discounts your presence next time.} },
{ t => 'The seam detector', p => 'List the three signals that a pub conversation has reached your natural seam: conversational, group-dynamic, and time-based.', a => q{Model: the story just completed (conversational); the group is splitting into new pairs (dynamic); your one drink is finished and the next round is forming (time). Leave ON a completed story — never mid-story, never after the third "one more".} },
{ t => 'The venue-currency audit', p => 'Think of one story you tell differently in different rooms. Write the pub version and the work version in one sentence each.', a => q{The craft is tonal translation: "I once deleted the wrong database" is a Pub Story with chaos and laughter; at work it is an Incident Retrospective with timelines. Same facts, different grammar — knowing which venue you are in is half of social intelligence.} },
